# Generated or fetched, never committed. See WORKFLOW.md section 11.
# Symlinks onto the project filesystem, made by scripts/link_storage.sh. Matched without a
# trailing slash, which git reads as "a directory only" and a symlink is not one.
data/raw
data/cache
results/
.snakemake/
benchmarks/
logs/
report/tables/
report/figs/
# Everything pdflatex leaves behind. The report is a generated artifact like any other: it is
# rebuilt by `rule all` from results/, and a committed PDF is a number that can drift from the run
# that produced it.
report/report.pdf
report/report.aux
report/report.bbl
report/report.blg
report/report.log
report/report.out
report/report.toc
scratch/
.scratch
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The talk website (talk/PLAN.md). Its node dependencies and its build output are generated;
# `talk/public/` is the one deliberate exception to "results are never committed", because the
# site is built on GitHub's runners where results/ does not exist (talk/PLAN.md section 4).
talk/node_modules/
talk/dist/
